Feature: EN 1994 structural scene
  The composite snapshot and its check report project to a locale-free 3D scene, 2D diagrams and drag handles.
  Every spatial part, every governing diagram and every editable dimension is reproduced by an independent library.

  Further specification assertions, asserted by the Rust unit tests of the crate and not by the platform adapters:
  - The default building projects a valid scene: Given the default EN 1994 snapshot and its settled check report When the structural scene is projected Then the scene passes the structural scene validation without violations And it contains the steel section, slab, effective-width ghost, sheeting, stud zones, transverse bars, neutral-axis plane, supports and loads of every beam And it contains the steel and concrete bodies with reinforcement of every column and the slab, sheeting and bars of every slab strip And two projections of the same revision have byte-identical canonical JSON
  - Plastic neutral axis at <eta> equals the brentq solution of the fibre equilibrium: Given a composite section HEB300 with the slab of the default beam When the plastic neutral axis is computed at a degree of shear connection <eta> Then the concrete block depth and the steel compression depth equal the scipy solution within 1e-7 Examples (3 rows: 0-4, 0-7, 1-0)
  - Every stud row is drawn as its own fastener with grips: Given a document whose beam carries <count> stud rows, <twins> of them at the position of another When the scene is projected Then one fastener entity exists per row bound to the per-stud check and the stud rows at one position share one station and spread over the flange And the handle list holds a position, a diameter and a height grip per row Examples (2 rows: 52 0, 52 1)
  - Stud load-slip, rib profile and slender columns equal the independent formulas: Given the stud law, the trapezoidal rib profile and the buckling curve a When the diagram values are written to the oracle Then numpy reproduces the Ollgaard-Slutter-Fisher load and its inverse And the rib polyline length equals the trapezoid dimension sum And the chi values equal EN 1993-1-1 6.3.1.2
  - Composite column polygon area equals the shapely area: Given the default concrete-filled column When its M-N interaction diagram is built Then the shapely area of the polygon equals the shoelace sum of the table twin
  - Handle <handle> edits <path>: Given the default EN 1994 snapshot When the handle "<handle>" is dragged to the parameter <s> Then the resolved write targets "<path>" with the value <value> Examples (5 rows: beam-b1-span-10-0-beams-id-beam-b1-spanm-10-0, beam-b1-stud-rows-2-4-beams-id-beam-b1-studs-countperrib-2, beam-b1-orientation-0-9-beams-id-beam-b1-sheeting-ribsparall, col-c1-size-0-15-columns-id-col-c1-outersizem-0-3, slab-s1-span-3-0-slabs-id-slab-s1-spanm-3-0)
  - Failing documents are red and carry failure glyphs: Given a beam of 16 m with 4 studs, a column with 9000 kN and a slab of 6 m When the scene is projected Then at least one entity has failing utilisation and a hatch And a failure glyph annotation exists
  - composite beams carry stations along their length: Given a continuous two-span composite beam When the scene is projected Then the steel member is coloured per check station and the studs differ by their utilisation And the cracked zone spans the contraflexure points of the kernel statics at 0.375 and 0.625 of the total length And the deflection line equals the closed form of a uniformly loaded span within 0.2 %
  - the mode track scrubs column buckling and girder lateral-torsional buckling one layer at a time: Given the unpropped building with a composite column and an unpropped girder When the scene is projected Then a "mode" track of kind Mode snaps over indices 1 to 2 with one mode layer per keyframe And the column load equals the Euler load of its effective stiffness and the girder moment equals the closed-form critical moment of a fork-ended I section under uniform moment And a document with a single mode gets no mode entities and no track
  - Slip along the studs is antisymmetric about midspan and checked against the slip capacity: Given a committed document with one simply supported composite beam When the diagrams of the beam are projected Then the slip diagram is zero at midspan and has opposite signs at the two supports And its support marker is bound to the stud resistance check and its table twin lists the slip per position
  - Encased columns carry a coloured fire temperature plate scrubbed by the fire track: Given an encased column with the fire rating R60 When the scene is projected Then the column has a plate with one temperature field per fire minute up to 60 And the surface is hotter than the core in every field And a "fire" track of kind Time has one keyframe per field And filled columns and unrated documents have no plate and no track
  - The slip arrows and the slip diagram share one law: Given a committed document with one simply supported composite beam When the slip arrows are sampled along the studs Then every arrow slip equals the slip diagram value at its station And the arrow lengths scale with the slip over the capacity of 6 mm
  - Hogging slabs carry a crack-width colour band: Given a two-span composite beam with EI2 over 15 % of each span When the scene is projected Then the band over the support holds the crack-control utilisation at the support and the support moment line of the PyNite model falls to 0.44996 at a quarter of the zone
  - Bridge girders show their end plate: Given a bridge girder with a declared end plate When the scene is projected Then an end plate entity is bound to the bearing check and three handles write the end plate width, height and the end zone length
  - Out-of-range materials raise a failure glyph: Given a beam with a concrete strength of 90 MPa When the scene is projected Then the failure glyph "beam-B1:failure-materials" exists exactly when the check "en1994.3.materials.beam-B1" fails or warns
  - The slab reinforcement grip writes the area per metre: Given the default EN 1994 snapshot When the handle "slab-S1:rebar-area" is dragged from 0 to half the strip width Then the resolved write targets "slabs[id=slab-S1].asM2PerM" with the values 0 and 4 % of the slab thickness
  - Every evaluated design case has a result diagram: Given the twelve catalogue demo cases When the diagrams are projected Then each case with results has a "case-results" diagram whose markers are bound to existing checks
